      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="1195" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">DGL (AT1G05800) is a DAD1 (AT2G44810) homolog. Its phospholipase A1 activity was demonstrated in vitro. In the in vitro assay, DGL was also shown had galactolipase activities towards DGDG and MGDG. The activities with DGDG and MGDG were 3 fold higher and 20% lower, respectively, when compared with the substrate phosphatidylcholine. DGL and DAD1 are the only two phospholipase A1 enzymes involved in jasmonic acid biosynthesis.</Comment>
